<!--Post: 4416--><!--Time: 1106339018-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4416"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 12:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Recently found a post from someone on another site about the Orange Coast Killer, or the Original Night Stalker &#40;as in, before Richard Ramirez.&#41; - take your pick.  <BR> <BR>I personally get tired of seeing so many people try to tie BTK in with other killers, but when I read up a bit on this one I felt it was worth pointing out.  <BR> <BR>The Original Night Stalker has enough similarities in his MO to compare and contrast, even though I strongly doubt he is the same killer. He bound his victims with special knots - in this case not buntline hitch knots but &#39;diamond&#39; knots - he had total control of the crime scenes, he cut the phone lines, he left very little evidence behind. There was a marked sadomasochistic element to his murders &#40;rem. BTK and his &#34;bondage master sadist tendencies&#34;&#41;. His physical description was not so different from some of the BTK descriptions, but he was perhaps younger at the time and in very good shape, physically. He targeted lower-risk victims just like BTK, but ONS&#39;s were &#39;higher-dollar&#39; professionals - he seemed to kill more than his share of people associated with the medical field, and a woman whose husband was hospitalized at the time of her murder as well. I already suspect, from what reading I&#39;ve done in a day and a half, that ONS had some connection to the field of medicine. Like BTK he was unafraid of dealing with more than one vic - in fact, he seemed to prefer killing couples.  <BR> <BR>ONS did not taunt the press that I know of - he preferred to take it to the victim. The most comprehensive site I&#39;ve found on him is this one; <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.ear-ons.com/" target=_top>http://www.ear-ons.com/</a>. If you go to the index page, there is a slightly silly-looking digitally rendered portrait of the killer in a ski mask, looking utterly crazed. If you click on that portrait, you will hear a phone call he left on one of his rape-only victims&#39; machines. It&#39;s terrifying, if you ask me. Don&#39;t listen to it late at night, alone in the dark.  <BR> <BR>Here is the other thing I wanted to point out about this, and this is more than relevant to BTK;  <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.ocsd.org/" target=_top>http://www.ocsd.org/</a> <BR> <BR>The Orange County Sheriff&#39;s Department&#39;s pages on this killer <i>&#40;just scroll down on their main page to the link in red that says &#39;serial killer update&#39;&#41;</i> are a model of how to engage the public in a manner that does not compromise their investigation and still encourages people looking at the info they have to do their own work on this unsolved series of killings. Wichita PD needs to look at how carefully rendered these OCSD pages are and do the same. It&#39;s one of the smartest things I&#39;ve seen a police department do in a situation like this.  <BR> <BR>The final thing I&#39;d like to note is the profile of the Original Night Stalker. What has stayed with me for a bit now is the feeling that the profiles are so comparable that perhaps a study of ONS may shed a little light in some dark corners in one&#39;s understanding of BTK. ONS inevitably seems to have had his own quirks - he actually brought his dog to at least a couple of crime scenes - but I still think that even if they are not the same killer, the comparison between them might be educational.  <BR> <BR>And if you follow those links and do think you&#39;re looking at BTK&#39;s more advanced work, after he&#39;d learned a few lessons and refined his methods, I&#39;d like to hear about that, too. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4416-->
<!--Post: 4422--><!--Time: 1106349708-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4422"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 3:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Steve, nice work on a case which doesn&#39;t get the interest it deserves. ONS is by far the scariest serial killer in US history, IMO. I&#39;ve known about him for a while but half a year ago, in Zodiac Chat, Tom also opined that this guy was colder-than-cold so I immediately sought the profile, have probably read it four times since then, and I finally discovered the site you link, a couple of months ago. <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t think he&#39;s BTK as ONS was capable of sex to completion inside a woman and I don&#39;t think BTK can do this. ONS also seems to know his attack areas too well for it to be BTK, ONS attacks at night, BTK during the day and before he was ONS, he was EAR who raped approximately sixty women. Again, BTK would not be capable of this, in my opinion. <BR> <BR>I agree completely that ONS is an excellent resource for study. Right now he&#39;s the only serial killer I&#39;m aware of who resembles BTK in any way. Is it possible to link the profile? And did you sense, as I had when reading the profile, that even hardcore LE types were slightly unnerved? I felt a sense of, &#34;This guy is incredibly dangerous.&#34; I agree with you that the phone call is straight from Satan, and it&#39;s the type of call women hate most. My good news is in my belief that ONS is dead or in prison, in that order. I know the same was said of BTK but this is a gut reaction of mine. Yes, ONS should be studied. No question. I don&#39;t think it so but if he&#39;s out there, there isn&#39;t a more dangerous killer in the entire country.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4422-->
<!--Post: 4435--><!--Time: 1106359454-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4435"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsbarn<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsbarn<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 6:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree with George about this not being BTK, but there are similarities, including the timeframe &#40;EAR/ONS raped a 16 year old girl on March 18, 1977 and Shirley Vian was killed on March 17, 1977&#41;and the possible military and university connections. Neither attacked in the summer of 1977.  EAR/ONS built up to murder through a series of rapes.  I think it is likely BTK must have a similar history that has not been tied to him, although the number of victims may not be as high. There seems to be an attraction to having another male who becomes a victim or children present as well.  Additionally, from the profile of Original Night Stalker: <BR>  <BR>Target Neighborhoods <BR> <BR>    Suspect primarily targeted middle-class to upper-middle class neighborhoods with homes on or near cul de sacs or homes adjacent to vacants fields, schools, parks, creeks or homes under construction. Several of the neighborhoods targeted by the suspect had &#34;homes for sale&#34; or homes recently sold. Suspect is known to have posed as a realtor, building inspector or prospective home-buyer. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.ear-ons.com/investigate7.html" target=_top>http://www.ear-ons.com/investigate7.html</a> <BR> <BR>This sort of angle has been brought up repeatedly with BTK. <BR> <BR>What do you make of the witness descriptions of two young men? &#40;After these sketches were released on March 16, 1978, the Sacremento rapes stopped, I guess causing investigators to feel they were on to something with these descriptions&#41;. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.ear-ons.com/composites.html" target=_top>http://www.ear-ons.com/composites.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4435-->
<!--Post: 4442--><!--Time: 1106364335-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4442"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 7:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><i>&#34;EAR/ONS built up to murder through a series of rapes.&#34;</i> This is the main reason I believe ONS isn&#39;t BTK; it&#39;s not even close. Of all known BTK murder victims, <i>none</i> were traditionally sexually penetrated, indicating strongly that BTK is sexually dysfunctional. For the same reason, I can&#39;t see BTK as a serial rapist who &#34;graduated&#34; to serial killer. It happens - in fact it happened with ONS - but I don&#39;t see it happening with BTK. I don&#39;t see BTK raping to completion even once.  <BR> <BR>ONS <i>always</i> sexually penetrated victims, and did so to completion as the crime scenes demonstrate. This is a huge difference which I say is enough to eliminate BTK as the ONS. Enough of my sophistry, I&#39;ll ask a pro who knows matters which the rest of us don&#39;t. Mike Kelleher really is a boon to this website.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4442-->
<!--Post: 4451--><!--Time: 1106369468-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4451"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 8:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George, you&#39;ve nailed why I concluded ONS wasn&#39;t the same guy, pretty quickly. In the sense you described, he was more sexually &#34;mature&#34; than BTK. BTK&#39;s offenses, sexually speaking, spoke of a more voyeuristic, immature sexuality. ONS was an aggressively physical rapist. BUT, the other commonalities are striking enough for me to think he&#39;s a killer to really learn about - that he and BTK are two variations on a very particular sort of serial killer - call him mostly organized to mixed, call him power-control, but either way they are peas in a pod. I think the biggest differences in the two were how adequate they probably seemed in daily life. I have a feeling ONS was a much more presentable sort, probably more a Ted Bundy-type on the outside; charming, witty, charismatic. BTK, I am convinced, has always been and still is the man everyone knows of but nobody really knows, and they have just a creepy enough impression of him to not want to try. In his everyday life, much more of a non-entity.  <BR> <BR>On the inside, though...their makeups were remarkably similar. If ONS is still alive, he is following BTK&#39;s resurgence, I&#39;d bet, with a passionate-seeming interest.  <BR> <BR>I do not know what to make of the two men; the very odd and chilling thought crossed my mind that two guys formed a team of sorts after meeting in the AF and one was the dominant &#39;actor&#39; in the crimes while the other was a voyeur, a lookout - wouldn&#39;t be the first time. There&#39;s no evidence I know of for that, though - it&#39;s raw, unsupported speculation on my part.  <BR> <BR>George, I have to agree - that recording is one of the most scary things I&#39;ve heard. How did the recipient sleep after that? How do they still? If this guy is still around, you&#39;re right, he&#39;s one of the most dangerous killers out there, hands down.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4451-->
<!--Post: 4453--><!--Time: 1106370055-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4453"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 9:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Oh, and thank you both for the responses so far. This forum gives one hope that smart, sane people are actually studying BTK as well.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4453-->
<!--Post: 4459--><!--Time: 1106377176-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4459"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 21, 2005 - 10:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Steve, thanks. Mr. Kelleher&#39;s new addition to the original profile seems to say that BTK wasn&#39;t sexually dysfunctional and I won&#39;t argue with Mr. Kelleher. I still think the two killers are different people, if only because of geography &#40;ONS struck in <i>much</i> wealthier neighborhoods than did BTK&#41;. Also BTK attacked by day, ONS by night. Finally, ONS usually &#40;possible always&#41; used blunt force trauma to dispatch his victims. BTK strangled, once stabbed, once shot but didn&#39;t kill. I recall two of the blunt force tools used by ONS were a sprinkler head and a fire log. BTK never approached this form of death. &#40;Although Bundy did.&#41; ONS drove hundreds of miles, whereas BTK could take a bus or ride a bicycle to his crime scenes. And I still find it interesting that of the proposed &#34;names&#34; for BTK, three of the nine include the word &#34;Wichita.&#34;  <BR> <BR>And he&#39;s only murdered in Wichita. There is something in BTK&#39;s psyche about Wichita. I&#39;m not glorifying a madman but the guy, to use newer terminology, I&#39;d rate as &#34;significantly above average&#34; when it comes to intelligence. The newer scale, I think, is something like average, above average, significantly above average, gifted. I don&#39;t know if gifted is the pinnacle or not. In thirty-one years he&#39;s only killed in Wichita. That <b>must</b> mean something. I&#39;m using solely definite BTK victims as opposed to possible victims. Do you think it unusual that in thirty-one years BTK has only killed in Wichita? I could be overreacting to this, I have Wichita&#39;s 1970 population at 349,600 and that figure includes suburbs. Maybe that&#39;s large enough for BTK, but for some reason BTK&#39;s sole use of Wichita seems a little odd to me. Thanks, gotta run. <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4459-->
<!--Post: 4464--><!--Time: 1106393099-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4464"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 22, 2005 - 3:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Isnt it strange that ONS and BTK asr both suspected of being in the Air Force. Man, there just rollin out the serial killers.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4464-->
<!--Post: 4486--><!--Time: 1106417800-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4486"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Chiquitah<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Chiquitah<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 22, 2005 - 10:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tom, sorry if this in the wrong place, but I wanted to respond to Nugzter. <BR> <BR>I know some guys that were in Vietnam, South America, etc, basically trained as assassins for the U.S. Military. They only know how to survive. <BR> <BR>Now, when they get back into &#34;society&#34; they need to get help to re-adjust. <BR> <BR>Some don&#39;t, and that could be why we end up with BTK&#39;s and EAR-ONS. <BR> <BR>Please don&#39;t take this wrong, as I am sure not all SK&#39;s have a military background. Nor am I saying all military turns out to be SK&#39;s.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4486-->
<!--Post: 5748--><!--Time: 1107323802-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5748"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 9:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->For one who is sure BTK and ONS are different people, I keep coming back here! It&#39;s tempting to consider them one and the same. I still think they are unrelated. But something very basic has been overlooked. California LE has DNA from ONS. WPD has DNA from BTK. I really hope that the DNA has been compared. Then we&#39;d know if they are the same.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5748-->
<!--Post: 5757--><!--Time: 1107350653-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5757"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Juno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Juno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 5:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Steve_huff said: <BR> <BR>&#34;If you click on that portrait, you will hear a phone call he left on one of his rape-only victims&#39; machines. It&#39;s terrifying, if you ask me. Don&#39;t listen to it late at night, alone in the dark.&#34; <BR> <BR>I&#39;ll second that!  I listened to that late at night after everyone was in bed, after having read the info on the same site earlier in the day.  Needless to say, I was up for most of the night.  That is probably THE creepiest thing I have ever heard. <BR> <BR>Was that call left on a victim&#39;s answering machine?   <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5757-->
<!--Post: 5782--><!--Time: 1107368723-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5782"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bodycheck<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bodycheck<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 02, 2005 - 10:25 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I listened to it too...FREAKY... <BR>what was it he said right at the end... <BR>I couldnt pick it up.... <BR> <BR>sounded to me ...like the guy was pulling his pud and repeating &#34;kill you&#34; over and over til right at the end.... <BR> <BR>i do admit though...If i got a msg like that on my machine....Id be VERY VERY armed. <BR> <BR>B <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5782-->
<!--Post: 6972--><!--Time: 1108099647-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6972"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 9:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->There are similarities between the BTK Strangler and the East Area Rapist/ Southern California Killer concerning modus operandi. It does not indicate the activities of the same individual. The victimology is an important matter. The East Area Rapist/ Southern California Killer was comfortable controlling and murdering affluent professionals. The BTK Strangler would be afraid to attack the bourgeoisie. He derives gratification from murdering urban proletariat women and the occasional man who happens to be at the crime scene.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6972-->
<!--Post: 7000--><!--Time: 1108116282-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7000"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 2:04 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK and EAR are not the same person. I doubt that they even knew of each other. EAR only really left one tip that could have identified him. That was when he told a victim &#34;I saw you at the Officer&#39;s club the other night.&#34; SSO was never able to make a connection. As to &#34;affluent professionals&#34; that was not what EAR targeted while in the Sacramento area, with a couple of exceptions. The sketches of the two individuals are in relation to a vicious double murder, and may or may not be connected to EAR. Area and basic description are similar. Motive could be completely unconnected to EAR, although I am willing to accept that it could have been connected, based upon recent information as to logistics. As to the suggestion that EAR had some connection to the field of medicine, that has been suggested. At this time the best count available is that EAR committed at least 42, and as many as 50 rapes in the Sacramento and Contra Costa County areas between June, 1976 and June, 1979. 60 is a little high. There is also the problem that EAR-ONS is very unique in that he &#34;graduated&#34;. This is not seen in BTK. He may have started with the requisite &#34;little stuff&#34; that is accepted dogma for this type of offender, but no one has shown the existence of such activity. BTK have have killed in the commission of his first felony, completely unlike EAR, as far as we know.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7000-->
<!--Post: 7036--><!--Time: 1108142950-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7036"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:linnieskid@earthlink.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Linnieskid<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Linnieskid<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 9:29 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nightrider:  Interesting side note, I lived in Sacramento during the early and mid 70&#39;s-Rancho Cordova &#40;on Tuollumne&#41; in 1977-78 and in Ventura in Ondulando, where one of his &#34;graduated&#34; murders took place. <BR>Each of my apts. and homes was approximately 2 blocks from where he &#34;hit&#41;.  I have often wondered if he was related in some way to my occupation or had a job like myself that transferred him.  I swear it was as if he followed me. I called the tip line in Sacramento but they couldn&#39;t have been less interested; I swear I heard the detective yawn. While in Rancho I had several close calls and was stalked, someone broke into my home and had a peeping tom. I know it is far fetched but I will always wonder if I knew him. &#40; I did see the peeper&#41;  By the grace of God...I also had a very close call with Gerald Gallego.  No on should wonder why I am so intrigued by all of this!  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7036-->
<!--Post: 7089--><!--Time: 1108176902-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7089"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 6:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Correct, Nightdriver; between 42 and 50. I&#39;m trying to remember where I read the number as sixty. At any rate, they aren&#39;t the same person.  <BR> <BR><i>He [BTK] may have started with the requisite &#34;little stuff&#34; that is accepted dogma for this type of offender</i> Not blindly accepted by me, although usually a lesser crime&#40;s&#41; precedes a more serious one of course. I do believe that Otero was his first homicide&#40;s&#41; and find it quite plausible that BTK has no criminal record. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7089-->
<!--Post: 7110--><!--Time: 1108187114-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7110"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 11, 2005 - 9:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wanted to clarify here that I&#39;ve never suggested that BTK and ONS are the same killer. I just think that knowing one is instructive to some degree when knowing the other. I would say the same thing about Harvey Glatman, whom BTK mentioned himself.  <BR> <BR>And I must admit, I find the fact that ONS was never caught and appeared to go to ground just like BTK every bit as disturbing as BTK&#39;s supposed disappearance, or &#39;retirement.&#39;  <BR> <BR>A third point that it&#39;s necessary to make is about the way the Orange County Sheriff has handled disseminating info on ONS - <i>their</i> page is one of the best you can find on the killer!  <BR> <BR>No, we can&#39;t say that the OC Sheriff&#39;s being much more open than the Wichita PD with what they know about this case has led to ONS&#39;s capture, but it is impressive and worthy of notice. It may very well lead to something, for all we know. I just think that more disclosure of certain evidence might lead to better tips where BTK is concerned. I&#39;d err on the side of releasing as much of his written material as is feasible. In the age of the internet, this could lead to any number of scenarios. And there&#39;s always the example of how the Unabomber was caught...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7110-->
<!--Post: 7145--><!--Time: 1108232248-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7145"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 10:17 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Linnieskid, thanks for posting over on A&amp;E. Your story is just the kind of untold story that will solve some cold cases. It did raise some eyebrows. Did you see the replies? I take that you were living there on Tuolumne when the Oct. 1, 1977 rape occured? As to Gallego, you&#39;ve already had enough close encounters for a lifetime. I was thinking about what I said last night about them not even knowing of the other&#39;s existence. I still think that&#39;s true, but it depends on when BTK was in the service. We don&#39;t know if he was stationed out here or overseas. But it was probably long before 1976. Of course he could have been out in Calif. for other reasons around 1976-1981. EAR is only about 54 max, today. If he&#39;s still around I&#39;d say they are both watching and getting a big laugh. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7145-->
<!--Post: 7177--><!--Time: 1108260208-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7177"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 6:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Steve_Huff, right on with Orange County Sheriff&#39;s Office and how they&#39;ve disseminated information re: ONS. I can&#39;t imagine a better proactive model. I&#39;d bet some at WPD are and possibly have been of the opinion that more information should be released. If there is internal strife at WPD, I hope that differences may be put aside for the sake of capturing BTK.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7177-->
<!--Post: 7209--><!--Time: 1108278505-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7209"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:linnieskid@earthlink.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Linnieskid<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Linnieskid<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 12, 2005 - 11:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nightdriver: I just couldn&#39;t hold it any longer. Even if no one listens I had to talk about it. It&#39;s the kind of thing you try to push out of your mind.  I thought the description might help and hopefully it will.I know that btk and ear are not the same. They probably don&#39;t know about each other.   I agree with you, I&#39;ve had enough contact for a lifetime...I pray ear is not watching because I do not think he&#39;d be laughing at my post and description of him.  Too creepy, perhaps I should be more careful about what I post.  Is Archangel76 le?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7209-->
<!--Post: 7374--><!--Time: 1108432813-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7374"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 6:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Another similarity between the BTK Strangler and the East Area Rapist is the psychopathic desire to control and manipulate the public. In October 1976, the Sacramento County Sheriff&#39;s Office held several informal and unpublicized public meetings to inform concerned citizens seven unsolved rapes occurred in the East Area of Sacramento since June 1976. At one meeting a man announced to the gathering he would not fear and challenged the East Area Rapist. He declared his family would not become victims of the rapist. The East Area rapist attacked his family shortly after the gatherings. The East Area Rapist did not appreciate the public dictating to him and the possible loss of control and domination. The BTK Strangler did not appreciate the speculation in January concerning the submission of another correspondence. He decided to submit the communication to a locale outside Wichita. The BTK Strangler would have been motivated by a desire to taunt the police, media and public like the East Area rapist. However, the BTK Strangler was motivated by the desire to avoid apprehension with intense media and public interest.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7374-->
<!--Post: 7402--><!--Time: 1108467013-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7402"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 3:30 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Linneskid: Someone listened, believe me. Your information is important. NO, I can&#39;t guarantee that he is not alive or not watching these crime boards, No one can. I think it&#39;s important to post as much info as possible to the public at large, they hold the key to solving this. I really think your perp was &#34;surfer bob&#34;. He hung out at Party Time, only about three miles away from where you lived. Unfortunately, no one has his real name. You may give anything you want to Arch through his web site, it will be secure. As to Arch being active LE, whatever he is he does not want made public at this time. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7402-->
<!--Post: 7403--><!--Time: 1108468570-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7403"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 3:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ivy_Leaguer: You may have a lot of your facts straight, but your interpretation of them is so backwards as to be laughable. Him showing up at the meeting and then attacking that guy 2 weeks later could have been a big &#34;oops, dammit&#34;. What if they held a recreation? Ala Cherrie Jo Bates? No, he realized how big a mistake that could have been, and he never did anything that stupid again. The only real similarity so far is that they both attacked their victims in or just outside their residences. I feel that EAR&#39;s gig was to strike fear in his victims, primarily females. I doubt that he really cared a hoot about what the general public thought about him. He was driven by his emming hatred of young attractive females. BTK seems to have picked his victims by some means no one is sure of yet.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7403-->
<!--Post: 7426--><!--Time: 1108492792-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7426"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:linnieskid@earthlink.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Linnieskid<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Linnieskid<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 10:39 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nightdriver, what was Party Time - a bar? I used to go to The Gold Mine Shaft &#40;partying and dancing&#41; and also went to Old Town forgot the name of the place, but I do remember that you had to go downstairs to enter, from the street..  &#40; the place in Old Town&#41; I&#39;ve been racking my lil ol pea brain.I wish I knew where I caught his attention. However it happened, I guarantee you I was followed over a period of time.  No incidents at all when I had a boyfriend staying with me. Forgive me if you stated this already but do you live or have you lived in Sacramento? I do understand if you don&#39;t want to answer. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7426-->
<!--Post: 7448--><!--Time: 1108500453-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7448"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bestbud<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bestbud<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 12:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Linnieskid, I think you are referring to The Steamboat...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7448-->
<!--Post: 7450--><!--Time: 1108501692-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7450"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:linnieskid@earthlink.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Linnieskid<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Linnieskid<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 1:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bestbud- Possibly. It was so long ago! Was there an &#34;underground ????&#34; night club?  Seems to me the title was Underground &#34;something&#34;. This was in the mid to late 70&#39;s. You must have lived in Sacramento area as well. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7450-->
<!--Post: 7453--><!--Time: 1108503294-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7453"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bestbud<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bestbud<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 1:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yep!  The Underground was in Old Town, too.  I was born and raised in Sacramento. Lived in Rosemont which was like 5 minutes away from Rancho Cordova.  Been in Wichita for a little over 4 years now...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7453-->
<!--Post: 7462--><!--Time: 1108506698-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7462"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 2:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The comparison between the East Area Rapist and the BTK Strangler may seem laughable and ridiculous on a superficial level. The desire to assert control and domination was evident in both attacks. Sadistic psychopaths crave control and domination. They find it difficult when someone challenges their understanding of the world and attempt to restore their perception of equilibrium. <BR> <BR>The East Area Rapist was an intelligent, meticulous and well organized offender. I doubt the attack was random. He would have used the two weeks to stalk the victims and conduct surveillance of the residence. The unknown subject sent the message to the community he would accept the challenge and instil fear in his victims and the community. The unknown subject may not have expressed his desire to taunt the public through letters, it does not suggest he did not derive gratification from the community&#39;s fear. <BR> <BR>The recreation of the October 1966 murder of Cheri Jo Bates at Riverside City College library in Riverside, California would be simpler than recreating a public gathering in Sacramento, California. Most of the people at the Riverside City College library were students and library staff. It would be more diffciult to identify a group of anonymous people who attended a public gathering a few weeks before a sexual attack.  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7462-->
<!--Post: 7474--><!--Time: 1108511884-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7474"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:linnieskid@earthlink.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Linnieskid<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Linnieskid<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 3:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ivy_leaguer, No the comparison is not at all ridiculous! They are both stalkers, and well organized and have a reasonable level of intelligence and are sooo very bold. I think most serial offenders share many common traits. <BR>Motivational factors are probably not the same. However; I do believe rapists crave and demand control domination and feed off of fear.  Unlike BTK, EAR had no desire to control the public&#40;only his victims&#41; No comuniques with media etc.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7474-->
<!--Post: 7478--><!--Time: 1108514085-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7478"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:linnieskid@earthlink.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Linnieskid<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Linnieskid<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 4:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bestbud  <BR>please go to the website, <a href="http://www.ear-ons.com" target=_top>www.ear-ons.com</a> <BR>Please read descriptions and if you &#34;recognize&#34; anyone at all please email this site. You lived in the general vicinity of where the EAR hit, and I believe, lived. <BR>Also, refer to my description post at aetv.com, cold cases, original night stalker. Does the description ring any bells?  It is imperative that any information no matter how seemingly inconsequential be posted.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7478-->
<!--Post: 7509--><!--Time: 1108531826-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7509"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 9:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ivy_Leaguer, I&#39;m not going to argue similarities any longer. EAR-ONS is considered by most to be very unique among serial rapists, so how can you possibly compare him to BTK? We don&#39;t know if BTK practiced with the small stuff, honed his art of killing overseas in the service, or started with the Oteros. You need much more on him to make any comparison. We don&#39;t even know if all of the crimes committed by EAR are known. What else might he have done? <BR>As to EAR being that smart and well planned out, he doesn&#39;t hold a candle to BTK. He made so many small mistakes here in Sacramento, and maybe one in Contra Costa County in the early seventies, that he was more lucky than smart. I have been told exactly that by a deputy who was maybe 30 feet behind him, chasing him over fences. You don&#39;t seem to be aware of the Granite Bay possible. If that was him, he forgot his gloves, oops, and then he still couldn&#39;t get the sliding glass door open with his screwdriver. How about the &#34;yellow submarine&#39;? Parking that in an area of Carmichael 3 nights in a row, and not being seen. Then there&#39;s &#34;You are Jane Doe, aren&#39;t you?&#34; Then there&#39;s the Walnut and Winding attack. Just kick in the door, that house is kinda secluded. All there was was a 13 year old and a 15 year old home alone. &#34;Oh well, might as well have fun anyway.&#34; That one by itself, is so far afield from his target group, that people still question it being him. But SSO said it was back then. My impression after many years of looking at the areas involved, is that he went into an area with AT LEAST five potential targets scoped out. <BR>I have a big problem with what you said about the meeting. I never implied that he did not specifically target the guy who stood up and said that. Even though no one has ever really confirmed that it happened that way, Carol Daly thinks it did and said so. Also, the meeting was not announced widely, only in that specific target area, and was not to be reported on by the media. So how can you say he meant that attack to be a message? If so, it only reached about one hundred people out of about 450,000 living in the Northeast area. Yuo say it would have been difficult to recreeate that meeting. Hello, how do you think those people got there in the first place?? SSO knows how they got them there. All you would need is about half of them to attend a recreation. someone just might have remembered that young guy who was sitting in the next to last row, and someone saw him get into a say, green malibu out in the parking lot. That&#39;s more than what they seem to have by sitting on their duffs. <BR>What I&#39;m really trying to say is that any comparison between the two will be of absolutely no value in identifying either one, why bother?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7509-->
<!--Post: 7512--><!--Time: 1108533390-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7512"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 9:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Linnieskid: I had a strange feeling that you were leading up to saying what you said about being followed for quite some time. SSO says they checked the financial records of all the victims and found no commonality. But you probably didn&#39;t write a check when you went down to the clubs in Old Sac. did you? I wonder if WPD did run such a financial check on all the known and possible victims? <BR>Bestbud did live just South of you, across Folsom Blvd. Incidentally, no one ever reported an attack or even a stalking in that entire residential area. That&#39;s a huge area, about 3.5 square miles, and nothing. Some of us are still wondering why. The maps showing everything associated with BTK are clustered quite a bit more tightly than a map of EAR&#39;s activity. I wonder if there is something out there &#34;off the map&#34;. Oh, yes, I am a native and lifelong resident of Sac. Kinda getting tired of it, it&#39;s not the town I grew up in.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7512-->
<!--Post: 7513--><!--Time: 1108535510-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7513"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 10:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nightdriver, <BR> <BR>The comparison between the East Area Rapist and the BTK Strangler was limited to the act of restoring control in those two events. The comparison does not extend to the modus operandi, the signature, the motivation or the victimology. The East Area Rapist may have made errors, but they would be considered insigificant, otherwise he would have been apprehended. The BTK Strangler made several errors, particularly in the murder of Kathryn Bright. He did not believe Kevin Bright would accompany his sister and take his weapon. Committing violent crime is not a perfect science. Offenders cannot consider every factor in the commission of a crime. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7513-->
<!--Post: 7514--><!--Time: 1108536440-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7514"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 10:47 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;d like to know why the responses to Ivy Leaguer are so vehement in tone. This thread is starting to look like it could be found on ks.com. Regardless of subject I&#39;ve always felt Ivy presents what he/she says in a very neutral manner, yet Nightdriver, you are being very aggressive and borderline insulting with your replies. It&#39;s not that hard to argue a point without resorting to angry or ad hominem attacks, folks. <BR> <BR>Maybe there&#39;s bad blood I don&#39;t want to know about, but I&#39;m just posting this because I started this thread. I also think, by the way, that the argument is veering way off track. My point was simply that the knowledge of both killers is instructive. They do match a broadly defined type.  I do not believe they are the same person, and I do believe each followed his own distinct pattern of behavior that, known in detail, would clearly separate the two. Again, the Harvey Glatman comparison applies. The bondage, dominance, manipulation and control were all the same as BTK. There <b>are</b> broad patterns these guys follow. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7514-->
<!--Post: 7518--><!--Time: 1108541872-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7518"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 12:17 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ivy Leaguer, <BR> <BR>I can only admire your reserve. Seriously.  <BR> <BR>Keep up the highly informed posts, I enjoy reading them. Your recent profile is extremely impressive, as is mine. ;&#41; Really, you probably know that your lucid, educated and highly intelligent posts are going to bruise some egos, even though that isn&#39;t your intent at all. I was one such person; I&#39;m over it. Excellent posts. <BR> <BR>This site has become, hands down, the best on the Internet regarding BTK. Many good minds post here and we need them to continue posting! It&#39;s my belief that ONS may give some insight into BTK, <b>and</b> the second link in the original post is one which can be quickly read. Yes, I&#39;m repeating the importance of studying the Orange County Sheriff&#39;s Department as concerns the general public and the presentation of case data. In my armchair opinion, it&#39;s &#34;that&#34; important.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7518-->
<!--Post: 7524--><!--Time: 1108553781-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7524"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 3:36 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m sorry if my tone of writing is not acceptable to some. I don&#39;t feel as if it&#39;s necessary to write as though I&#39;m writing a master&#39;s thesis just to get my point across. Think of this: If you keep &#34;killing the messenger&#34;, you&#39;re never going to get the message. <BR>Ivy Leaguer: Thank you for clarifying what points of similarity you are looking at. However, I find the desire to exert control and domination over others to be present in a large percentage of the population. People like Larry Ellison, Al Davis and others I forget right now come to mind. I find that trait to be just a little too common and not necessarily a good enough indicator to be useful in making an identification. MO and sig. can be adjusted, in a effort to avoid detection. But I do agree that motivation, if truly determined in the case of one, could turn out to be similar in the case of the other. Victimology in the case of EAR seems to have progressed upwards, from twenty-somethings just starting out in life, up to mid-30&#39;s upper middle class professionals by 1986. That is, with the exceptions of the attacks upon minors. With BTK, it seems to be all over the map. starting out with a quadruple. I have a strange feeling that there is some sort of hint there. I am open to the suggestion that EAR in Sacramento and possibly Contra Costa, had made contact with some of his victims or members of their families. Not necessarily recent to the attacks, but at some time. I would not be surprised to see the same in BTK.  <BR>I do completely disagree with you on the severity of EAR&#39;s mistakes. Most could have been very fatal. He was very lucky in that regards. If indeed he was involved in the Maggiore murders, that was very stupid of him. Being seen walking in the neighborhood of the killings for at least 30 minutes without his requisite mask on, and then dropping a damn shoelace at the scene of the confrontation. That one shoelace is basically what has tied him to Maggiore for the last 27 years and 13 days. Also the taking of Woofy to one of his crimes in So Cal. Because of that, the real owners of Woofy were found and tied him to a Santa Barbara area gang called the Haskell Locals. We do not see any possible connection between BTK and any group of thugs, do we? Some minor similarities are present, I just don&#39;t feel they would lead to identification. that&#39;s what this is all about, isn&#39;t it?     <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7524-->
<!--Post: 7534--><!--Time: 1108563844-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7534"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 6:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nightdriver, <BR>A bit of rudeness did bother me but not as much as the thought of animosity needlessly developing between two very intelligent people - you and Ivy Leaguer. I&#39;ve also been sarcastic in the past but am much improved on that score. I hope that you and Ivy Leaguer will continue posting, as your IQ&#39;s are needed here. <BR> <BR>I&#39;ve read enough to consider you an expert in your knowledge of the EAR/ONS crimes. I wanted to add that while I believe profiling works, <u>if used correctly,</u> you&#39;re not alone in being skeptical about the art. Case in point, the profile of ONS at aetv.com. It&#39;s not exactly accurate and while it has probably been redacted, I agree that the profile&#39;s mention of things such as ONS was evidence-conscious, intelligent, and needed to appear macho are underwhelming at best. An average police detective would already know, within thirty seconds, these blatantly obvious aspects of the perp. The Goleta information is very probably an excellent example of how a profile can ruin a case. I enjoy your posts on the ONS board, I&#39;ve read a ton of &#39;em. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7534-->
<!--Post: 7558--><!--Time: 1108574310-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7558"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:linnieskid@earthlink.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Linnieskid<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Linnieskid<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 9:18 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nightdriver, I respect your insight.Do you conclude &#40;you know enough about my scenario to make a reasonable conclusion&#41;that I was followed &#40;stalked&#41;?  Would you consider my thinking down that avenue reasonable? I guess I am just looking for confirmation. I will probably always wonder...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7558-->
<!--Post: 7577--><!--Time: 1108584693-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7577"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 12:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George, thank you, I was not trying to get hostile. I was more concerned with skewing the profile by mis-interpreting or omitting what a specific profiler doesn&#39;t feel are relevant facts. I am not a critic of profiling. I did deride the use of geographic profiling in re EAR&#39;s Sacramento crimes. But that was strictly because that works best in real time. and they were suggesting that you just plug in real time data and apply it back to 1978. GIGO. In re Yates, I saw the geo maps on the web produced for that case and they were extremely close. They had his residence down to a half mile from where it really was.  <BR>Some people have questioned that FDLE profile on the grounds that it did not consider anything about his activities in Sacramento and Contra Costa. Many people are concerned about relying on profiles produced from afar with just paper data as input. As long as people realize that if the word on the street differs from the profile, you have to consider the accuracy of each, and go with what your gut tells you. <BR>Linneskid: I will have to go back over everything you&#39;ve posted, but right now, I think you were. the amount of intel he gathered in the Sacramento area would have kept anyone busy 8 hours a day, if done just by stalking around in bushes all night. He did have other ways of targeting people, you may have just hit upon one of those ways. Now, if only some more people like you would come forward, maybe a light would go on in someone&#39;s head. Oh, sorry, Party Time is a doughnut shop on the Northeast corner of Watt Ave. and Fair Oaks Blvd. It was one of the few open 24 hours back then. Lots of characters hung out at all of them.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7577-->
<!--Post: 7597--><!--Time: 1108593644-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7597"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 2:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->To Steve and George, <BR> <BR>I appreciate the kind comments. <BR> <BR>To Nightdriver, <BR> <BR>Your reservoir of knowledge on the East Area Rapist is superior to mine and analysis is more refined. I was not offended by the comments.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7597-->
